# philosophy: entoolment is the pinnacle

**tool** is the umbrella: 📚 brief, 💧 fluid, 🔩 rigid, 🪨 solid skill. all are pavement; they differ in imagine cost per use. `skill` is the word a brief is contrasted against, never `tool`.

**entoolment** is a direction on a ladder, not a binary. ask *"which rung, and can it climb one?"*

| rung | artifact | imagine cost per use |
|---|---|---|
| 0 | 🧠 tribal | full derivation |
| 1 | 📚 brief (prethought concepts) | read + interpret + apply |
| 2 | 💪💧 fluid skill (steps written, a brain walks them) | follow the steps |
| 3 | 💪🔩 rigid skill (some branches crystallized) | the probabilistic branches |
| 4 | 💪🪨 solid skill (one call) | none |

rungs 2-4 are rhachet's determinism spectrum (`harden`); **entool spans all five**.

## a higher rung never retires a lower one

*"we entooled it, delete the brief"* is a defect: the skill mechanized capacity, never the concept; a solid skill with no brief is a black box. move an artifact one rung; rung 3 is often the honest limit. 🗿 the most general rigid skill is a route.

limit: a tool that pretends determinism over a fluid process is confidently wrong at scale.
